🔹 How MLOps Differs from DevOps and SRE — and How You Can Transition into It
Technology keeps evolving — and just like DevOps revolutionized software delivery, MLOps is now transforming how we build, deploy, and manage machine learning models at scale.

But many engineers still ask —
 👉 How is MLOps actually different from DevOps or SRE?
 👉 Can I move into MLOps from my current DevOps role?

Let’s break it down simply 👇

DevOps — The Foundation
DevOps focuses on automating the software delivery process — CI/CD, version control, infrastructure automation, and monitoring.
It’s all about speed, collaboration, and continuous delivery.
Tools: Jenkins | Docker | Kubernetes | Terraform | GitHub Actions

SRE — The Reliability Expert
SRE ensures systems stay healthy, resilient, and observable in production.
It’s where performance meets automation and incident management.
Tools: Prometheus | Grafana | ELK | Python | Bash | Chaos Engineering

MLOps — The Next Evolution
MLOps extends DevOps principles to machine learning systems — managing the entire lifecycle from model training to deployment and monitoring.
It brings together Data Science, DevOps, and Cloud Engineering into one practice.
Tools: MLflow | Kubeflow | Airflow | AWS SageMaker | TFX | Vertex AI

